From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 08:59:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/74] fix(gastown): re-derive the step bead id at both
 decision points (gcp-rz8a)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review of the previous commit found the fix resting on an assumption the
formula cannot enforce: STEP_BEAD_ID was resolved once in step 1 and then used
several fenced blocks later. An agent that runs each block in its own shell
inherits nothing, so the final close would fall through to its WARN branch and
leave the step bead open — reintroducing the exact respawn loop the change
exists to prevent — while every command still exited 0.

Both blocks that decide whether bead state gets re-written now derive their own
ids: the already-submitted guard re-derives the convoy, work bead and step bead
before reading them, and the closing block re-resolves the step bead when the
variable is empty. This follows the convention mol-refinery-patrol already uses
for CURRENT_WISP, which re-derives per step rather than threading a variable
through the whole formula. A contract test pins both, shown red against the
previous commit's formula and green after.
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml    | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
index 38f23b2..93b26d8 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
@@ -340,6 +340,10 @@ substitute `$GC_BEAD_ID` here — for a polecat that is the convoy the molecule
 was poured on, not this step, and closing it would close work that is still
 live.
 
+Steps 2 and 10 re-derive both ids instead of inheriting them. Run each fenced
+block in its own shell and an inherited variable is empty, which for those two
+blocks degrades exactly into the failure this step is fixing.
+
 **2. Already-submitted guard (idempotent re-entry).**
 
 A re-entered submit-and-exit must not re-write bead state. Step 8 sets the
@@ -350,6 +354,15 @@ present — target recorded, branch on origin at this commit, and the bead hande
 to somebody who is not this session:
 
 ```bash
+# Re-derived rather than inherited: run each block in its own shell and the
+# guard silently degrades to "no evidence" — which is the wrong direction for
+# the one check standing between a respawn and a second pass over bead state.
+CONVOY_STATUS=$(gc convoy status {{convoy_id}} --json)
+WORK_BEAD_ID=$(printf '%s' "$CONVOY_STATUS" | jq -r 'if (.children | length) == 1 then .children[0].id else empty end')
+STEP_SESSION="${BEADS_ACTOR:-${GC_SESSION_NAME:-${GC_SESSION_ID:-${GC_AGENT:-}}}}"
+STEP_BEAD_ID=$(gc bd list --assignee="$STEP_SESSION" --status=in_progress \
+  --metadata-field gc.step_ref=mol-polecat-work.submit-and-exit \
+  --include-infra --limit=0 --json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '.[0].id // empty')
 SUBMITTED_JSON=$(gc bd show "$WORK_BEAD_ID" --json)
 SUBMITTED_TARGET=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].metadata.target // empty')
 SUBMITTED_BRANCH=$(printf '%s' "$SUBMITTED_JSON" | jq -r '.[0].metadata.branch // empty')
@@ -575,6 +588,15 @@ the work on its next poll.
 
 **10. Close this step bead, then signal the reconciler and exit.**
 ```bash
+if [ -z "${STEP_BEAD_ID:-}" ]; then
+    # Step 1 resolved this already; re-resolve rather than trust it, because a
+    # block run in a fresh shell inherits nothing and an unresolved id here is
+    # exactly the open step bead this whole change exists to prevent.
+    STEP_SESSION="${BEADS_ACTOR:-${GC_SESSION_NAME:-${GC_SESSION_ID:-${GC_AGENT:-}}}}"
+    STEP_BEAD_ID=$(gc bd list --assignee="$STEP_SESSION" --status=in_progress \
+      --metadata-field gc.step_ref=mol-polecat-work.submit-and-exit \
+      --include-infra --limit=0 --json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '.[0].id // empty')
+fi
 if [ -n "$STEP_BEAD_ID" ]; then
     gc bd close "$STEP_BEAD_ID" --reason "submit-and-exit: branch pushed, work bead handed to the refinery"
 else
diff --git a/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh b/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
index 24d1426..04f4732 100755
--- a/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
+++ b/gastown/tests/test_gastown_pack_assets.sh
@@ -456,6 +456,25 @@ PY
     [[ "$submit_block" != *'gc bd close "$WORK_BEAD_ID"'* ]] ||
         fail "the polecat never closes the work bead; only the refinery does"
 
+    # An agent may run each fenced block in its own shell, so the two blocks
+    # that decide whether bead state gets re-written must derive their own ids
+    # rather than inherit them and silently degrade to "nothing to close".
+    python3 - "$formula" <<'PY' || fail "the guard and the close must re-derive their ids, not inherit them"
+import sys
+import tomllib
+
+data = tomllib.load(open(sys.argv[1], "rb"))
+step = next(s for s in data["steps"] if s["id"] == "submit-and-exit")
+text = step["description"]
+guard = text[text.index("**2. Already-submitted guard"): text.index("**3. Branch-shape gate")]
+close = text[text.index("**10."):]
+for block in (guard, close):
+    if "--metadata-field gc.step_ref=mol-polecat-work.submit-and-exit" not in block:
+        raise SystemExit(1)
+if "gc convoy status" not in guard:
+    raise SystemExit(1)
+PY
+
     # The close has to happen BEFORE the drain, or the reconciler kills the
     # session first and the step bead is left open exactly as before.
     python3 - "$formula" <<'PY' || fail "submit-and-exit must close its step bead before draining"
-- 
